<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:781407d7-99cd-4bc3-ab69-5b6090e53863> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:781407d7-99cd-4bc3-ab69-5b6090e53863> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 16 ;
    kg:section_id "781407d7-99cd-4bc3-ab69-5b6090e53863" ;
    kg:section_title "Elimination" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "The apparent terminal elimination half-life of empagliflozin was estimated to be 12.4 h and apparent oral clearance was 10.6 L/h based on the population pharmacokinetic analysis." .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:78b9d4fe-f485-4997-aff0-d1776b193837> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:78b9d4fe-f485-4997-aff0-d1776b193837> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 50 ;
    kg:section_id "78b9d4fe-f485-4997-aff0-d1776b193837" ;
    kg:section_title "Talk to your doctor, pharmacist or nurse before taking this medicine, and during treatment:" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text """- if you have 'type 1 diabetes'. This type usually starts when you are young and your body does not produce any insulin. You should not take Jardiance if you have type 1 diabetes.
- if you have serious kidney problems - your doctor may limit your dose to 10 mg once a day or ask you to take a different medicine (see also section 3, 'How to take Jardiance').
- if you have serious liver problems - your doctor may ask you to take a different medicine.
- might be at risk of dehydration, for example:
- o if you are being sick, have diarrhoea or fever, or if you are not able to eat or drink
- o if you are taking medicines that increase urine production [diuretics] or lower blood pressure
- o if you are 75 years old or older.""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7a8abc09-7c40-45e0-8ad5-f5972fe08693> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:7a8abc09-7c40-45e0-8ad5-f5972fe08693> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 46 ;
    kg:section_id "7a8abc09-7c40-45e0-8ad5-f5972fe08693" ;
    kg:section_title "17. UNIQUE IDENTIFIER - 2D BARCODE" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text "2D barcode carrying the unique identifier included." .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7a95181c-65e1-480a-b7eb-533cc58183dd> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:7a95181c-65e1-480a-b7eb-533cc58183dd> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 52 ;
    kg:section_id "7a95181c-65e1-480a-b7eb-533cc58183dd" ;
    kg:section_title "How much to take" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text """- The recommended dose of Jardiance is one 10 mg tablet once a day. If you have type 2 diabetes mellitus, your doctor will decide whether to increase your dose to 25 mg once a day, if needed to help to control your blood sugar.
- Your doctor may limit your dose to 10 mg once a day if you have a kidney problem.
- Your doctor will prescribe the strength that is right for you. Do not change your dose unless your doctor has told you to.""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7ae03919-8b67-4efd-8da4-8a93bed16280> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:7ae03919-8b67-4efd-8da4-8a93bed16280> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 15 ;
    kg:section_id "7ae03919-8b67-4efd-8da4-8a93bed16280" ;
    kg:section_title "DESCRIPTION" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """In the event of an overdose with JARDIANCE, consider contacting the Poison Help line (1-800-222-1222) or a medical toxicologist for additional overdosage management recommendations. Removal of empagliflozin by hemodialysis has not been studied.

10""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_DOCUMENT <urn:kg:jardiance:document:b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0> ;
    kg:DERIVED_FROM_SECTION <urn:kg:jardiance:section:7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b> ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 11 ;
    kg:section_id "7b001011-32f3-4040-b4ff-2baa77dee29b" ;
    kg:section_title "7 DRUG INTERACTIONS" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """See Table 4 for clinically relevant interactions with JARDIANCE.

Table 4 Clinically Relevant Interactions with JARDIANCE

| Diuretics                                            | Diuretics                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
|------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Clinical Impact                                      | Coadministration of empagliflozin with diuretics resulted in increased urine volume and frequency of voids, which might enhance the potential for volume depletion.                                                                                           |
| Intervention                                         | Before initiating JARDIANCE, assess volume status and renal function. In patients with volume depletion, correct this condition before initiating JARDIANCE. Monitor for signs and symptoms of volume depletion, and renal function after initiating therapy. |
| Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues                     | Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
| Clinical Impact                                      | The risk of hypoglycemia is increased when JARDIANCE is used in combination with insulin secretagogues (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin.                                                                                                                       |
| Intervention                                         | Coadministration of JARDIANCE with an insulin secretagogue (e.g., sulfonylurea) or insulin may require lower dosages of the insulin secretagogue or insulin to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia.                                                               |
| Lithium                                              | Lithium                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| Clinical Impact                                      | Concomitant use of an SGLT2 inhibitor with lithium may decrease serum lithium concentrations.                                                                                                                                                                 |
| Intervention                                         | Monitor serum lithium concentration more frequently during JARDIANCE initiation and dosage changes.                                                                                                                                                           |
| Positive Urine Glucose Test                          | Positive Urine Glucose Test                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| Clinical Impact                                      | SGLT2 inhibitors increase urinary glucose excretion and will lead to positive urine glucose tests.                                                                                                                                                            |
| Intervention                                         | Monitoring glycemic control with urine glucose tests is not recommended in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors. Use alternative methods to monitor glycemic control.                                                                                             |
| Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay | Interference with 1,5-anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| Clinical Impact                                      | Measurements of 1,5-AG are unreliable in assessing glycemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors.                                                                                                                                                      |""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7be759b0-c4fa-439c-a15e-c495d012756f> a kg:PISection ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
