Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001229 | Match Text: In patients with CKD, JARDIANCE slowed the eGFR decline across the spectrum of uACR | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised, parallel-group, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 6609 patients with CKD, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=3304) were evaluated vs placebo (n=3305). Patients were adults with an eGFR ≥ 20, < 45 mL/min/1.73 m2 ; or an eGFR ≥ 45, < 90 mL/min/1.73 m2 with a uACR ≥ 200 mg/g. The primary endpoint in the EMPA-KIDNEY trial was a composite of CV death or progression of kidney disease defined as end-stage kidney disease (the initiation of maintenance dialysis or receipt of a kidney transplant), a sustained decrease in the eGFR to <10 ml/min/1.73 m2, a sustained decrease in eGFR of ≥40% from baseline, or death from renal causes. Pati""" ;
