Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001244 | Match Text: Diabetes guidelines recommend early use of SGLT2is in patients with T2D regardless of metabolic parameters | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Guidelines | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In addition to comprehensive CV risk management  ASCVD has been defined differently across CVOTs but all included individuals with eCVD (eg, MI, stroke, any revascularisation procedure). Variably included: conditions such as transient ischaemic attack, unstable angina, amputation, symptomatic or asymptomatic coronary artery disease. A strong recommendation is warranted for people with CVD and a weaker recommendation for those with indicators of high CV risk. While definitions of high risk vary, most comprise ≥55 years of age with 2 or more additional risk factors (including obesity, hypertension, smoking, dyslipidaemia, or albuminuria). Current or prior symptoms of HF with documented HFrEF or HFpEF. eGFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 OR albuminuria (ACR ≥3.0 mg/mm""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

