<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2102be4a-d037-4724-b135-e0de418fa9e2> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "2102be4a-d037-4724-b135-e0de418fa9e2" ;
    kg:chunk_index 75 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 14 ;
    kg:section_id "3a1ea206-6d25-414f-be52-b5efee0d41df" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "fa0170b157a6ff32a269fbcb75ada0f76af0a0d2f5be3e63de810635a143c72b" ;
    kg:text """In glycemic control trials in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, a total of 2,721 (32%) patients treated with JARDIANCE were 65 years of age and older, and 491 (6%) were 75 years of age and older.  JARDIANCE is expected to have diminished glycemic efficacy in elderly patients with renal impairment [see Use in Specific Populations (8.6)] .  The risk of volume depletion-related adverse reactions increased in patients who were 75 years of age and older to 2.1%, 2.3%, and 4.4% for placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg. The risk of urinary tract infections increased in patients who were 75 years of age and older to 10.5%, 15.7%, and 15.1% in patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2) and Adverse Reactions (6.1)] .

In the EMPEROR-Reduced, EMPEROR-Preserved, and EMPA-KIDNEY trials, no overall differences in safety and effectiveness have been observed between patients 65 years of age and older and younger adult patients. EMPEROR-Reduced included 1,188 (64%) patients treated with JARDIANCE 65 years of age and older, and 503 (27%) patients 75 years of age and older. EMPEROR-Preserved included 2,403 (80%""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:210bca7f-6468-43cb-95cd-c413b5806ccb> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "210bca7f-6468-43cb-95cd-c413b5806ccb" ;
    kg:chunk_index 29 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 5 ;
    kg:section_id "4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "aeff78a4c03d1fe5b97a63082478d43787ce942a54461d54ef2747b8996b7f11" ;
    kg:text """Based on the mode of action of SGLT2 inhibitors, osmotic diuresis accompanying glucosuria may lead to a modest decrease in blood pressure (see section 5.1). Therefore, caution should be exercised in patients for whom an empagliflozin-induced drop in blood pressure could pose a risk, such as patients with known cardiovascular disease, patients on anti-hypertensive therapy with a history of hypotension or patients aged 75 years and older.

In case of conditions that may lead to fluid loss (e.g. gastrointestinal illness), careful monitoring of volume status (e.g. physical examination, blood pressure measurements, laboratory tests including haematocrit) and electrolytes is recommended for patients receiving empagliflozin. Temporary interruption of treatment with empagliflozin should be considered until the fluid loss is corrected.""" ;
    kg:token_count 210 .

