    kg:text """ratio

LVEF &gt;30%: Includes both above and below the median NT-proBNP. To be eligible for inclusion, patients with an LVEF &gt;30% were required to meet a higher NT-proBNP threshold than those with LVEF ≤ 30%, unless they additionally had a history of HHF within the past 12 months.""" ;
    kg:token_count 71 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5864a06b-70ba-4018-b4a4-29b4cc48e2ee> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "5864a06b-70ba-4018-b4a4-29b4cc48e2ee" ;
    kg:chunk_index 157 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 32 ;
    kg:section_id "aa122e32-acb0-4ed0-b8cb-402045f53ab7" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "b5859c44807e16c4ad5ea558be736ee1149fa22a9f7f2316a8c0950e6941a8be" ;
    kg:text """The primary endpoint in EMPA-REG OUTCOME was the time to first occurrence of a Major Adverse Cardiac Event (MACE).  A major adverse cardiac event was defined as occurrence of either a CV death or a non-fatal myocardial infarction (MI) or a non-fatal stroke.  The statistical analysis plan had pre-specified that the 10 and 25 mg doses would be combined.  A Cox proportional hazards model was used to test for non-inferiority against the pre-specified risk margin of 1.3 for the hazard ratio of MACE and superiority on MACE if non-inferiority was demonstrated. Type-1 error was controlled across multiples tests using a hierarchical testing strategy.

JARDIANCE significantly reduced the risk of first occurrence of primary composite endpoint of CV death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, or non-fatal stroke (HR: 0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99).  The treatment effect was due to a significant reduction in the risk of CV death in subjects randomized to empagliflozin (HR: 0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77), with no change in the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction or non-fatal stroke (see Table 15 and Figures 5 and 6).  Results for the 10 mg and 25 mg empagliflozin dosages were consistent with results for t""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

