    kg:text """1. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: NA
Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001160 | Match Text: JARDIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in the hospital | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054).  In the EMPULSE trial, the initiation of empagliflozin for acute HF produced clinical benefit regardless of the degree of symptomatic impairment at baseline and improved""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:65e6ce38-33bf-4887-8184-e1d3a60dc02c> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "65e6ce38-33bf-4887-8184-e1d3a60dc02c" ;
    kg:chunk_index 15 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 3 ;
    kg:section_id "6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "1f89ccfb19ce3c851cd740502201b3549435bd585126b6fbe3b8e222e9b0517b" ;
    kg:text """Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .

In patients with an eGFR &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg.

In patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, the glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is reduced in patients with an eGFR &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and likely absent in patients with an eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . Therefore, if eGFR falls below 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , additional glucose lowering treatment should be considered if needed (see sections 4.4, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).""" ;
    kg:token_count 153 .

