    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 1 ;
    kg:section_id "f9f1c2ed-a62f-44e4-b02c-6fa39df42688" ;
    kg:source_document_id "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc" ;
    kg:source_document_type "claims_content_modules" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx" ;
    kg:source_hash "4c493cb0d6afa69d080cf2a85ad0dbcc833edf63c21b86cbe80428e2dfbc61c4" ;
    kg:text "DIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in hospital within 1-5 days after stabilization | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%).  Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%).  In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054)." ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9ecfc3dd-3992-4f56-aef2-fd83eb05af11> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "9ecfc3dd-3992-4f56-aef2-fd83eb05af11" ;
    kg:chunk_index 12 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 5 ;
    kg:section_id "bf4f0bfc-226c-4422-abb3-b24a016dcd89" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "b7cac90fb20d4064fcbc999232cd73d4082a664917e47ad44a0f80ccdbbe5f4c" ;
    kg:text """to improve outcomes for all people living with T2D, CKD, and/or CVD* †

The proven cardiovascular benefits ‡  of JARDIANCE position it as a trusted and foundational choice across the CRM spectrum CV complications are the main cause of death in over 1 billion people who live with CRM conditions globally, highlighting the urgent need for early and foundational interventions like JARDIANCE

JARDIANCE provides broad protection by reducing risk for people living with CKD, HF , or T2D with eCVD.""" ;
    kg:token_count 124 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9ef017e4-7216-46d4-8f77-3a5488331806> a kg:Chunk ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:chunk_id "9ef017e4-7216-46d4-8f77-3a5488331806" ;
    kg:chunk_index 78 ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 14 ;
    kg:section_id "36c838fb-19f2-490d-aeec-391f25570fc0" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "56fa220ad783f7c4846e49da0321decbeed12c9054205e72e1867951bc8bc217" ;
    kg:text """adult patients with type 2 diabetes and established cardiovascular disease (eGFR greater than or equal to 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, in a total of 9,718 patients with heart failure (eGFR greater than or equal to 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPEROR-Reduced and EMPEROR-Preserved trials, and in 6,609 adult patients with chronic kidney disease (eGFR 20 to 90 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ) in the EMPA-KIDNEY study.  The safety profile across eGFR subgroups in these trials was consistent with the known safety profile [see Adverse Reactions (6.1) and Clinical Studies (14.3, 14.4, 14.5)].

Efficacy and safety trials with JARDIANCE did not enroll adult patients with an eGFR less than 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2  or on dialysis. Once enrolled, adult patients in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME, EMPERORReduced, EMPEROR-Preserved, and EMPA-KIDNEY trials were not required to discontinue therapy for worsening of eGFR to less than 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 or initiation of dialysis [see Clinical Studies (14.3, 14.4, 14.5)].""" ;
    kg:token_count 252 .

