Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000969 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and CVD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of CV death by 38% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analyzed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The 14% RRR in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p<0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77) and""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

