    kg:page_number 50 ;
    kg:section_id "78b9d4fe-f485-4997-aff0-d1776b193837" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:source_hash "d68a50a9bbd1da5aaf8ffd35b9efc79e9da01761ad4a1a4ee872c1973c827ca3" ;
    kg:text """- if you have 'type 1 diabetes'. This type usually starts when you are young and your body does not produce any insulin. You should not take Jardiance if you have type 1 diabetes.
- if you have serious kidney problems - your doctor may limit your dose to 10 mg once a day or ask you to take a different medicine (see also section 3, 'How to take Jardiance').
- if you have serious liver problems - your doctor may ask you to take a different medicine.
- might be at risk of dehydration, for example:
- o if you are being sick, have diarrhoea or fever, or if you are not able to eat or drink
- o if you are taking medicines that increase urine production [diuretics] or lower blood pressure
- o if you are 75 years old or older.""" ;
    kg:token_count 182 .

