    kg:source_document_id "e77ccb64-a3a2-41c2-9027-fb5e54716ebc" ;
    kg:source_document_type "claims_content_modules" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_Claims_updated & Content Modules 1.xlsx" ;
    kg:source_hash "2557be4f31022f1dd99126c508108f46551e31cf9b9bc0049a8749b7a8b37800" ;
    kg:text "F > 40%, JARDIANCE slowed the decline of renal function by 2 times | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety profile of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) was evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  The rate of decline in eGFR was a prespecified secondary outcome of the EMPEROR-Preserved trial.  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eGFR=estimated glomerular filtration rate; HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk red" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

<urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:dc07ff45-b52f-4e63-815b-f76df2c3df47> a kg:Chunk ;
