    kg:source_hash "f44ba55a7c37cc2bfbd365cc04b7cfd9e53abbe1d7a8be29fa575ce09b887274" ;
    kg:text "ere 75 years of age or older. 75.9% of the study population were White, 13.8% Asian and 4.3% Black/African American. At randomisation, 81.5% of patients were NYHA class II, 18.1% were class III and 0.3% were class IV. The EMPERORPreserved study population included patients with a LVEF &lt; 50% (33.1%), with a LVEF 50 to &lt; 60% (34.4%) and a LVEF ≥ 60% (32.5%). At baseline, the mean eGFR was 60.6 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and the median urinary albumin to creatinine ratio (UACR) was 21 mg/g. About half of the patients (50.1%) had an eGFR of ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 26.1% of 45 to &lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , 18.6% of 30 to &lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and 4.9% 20 to &lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 ." ;
    kg:token_count 171 .

