    kg:text """ass II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF > 40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint (HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001).  CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular;  HFpEF=heart failure with preserved ejection fraction; HHF=hospitalization for heart failure; HR=hazard ratio; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction;  NYHA=New York Heart Association; RRR=relative risk reduction. | Reference: RD-157961 Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461 | AMA Style Guide References: Anker SD, Butler J, Filippatos G, et al. N Engl J Med. 2021;385(16):1451-1461. | Content Modules & Rule Sets: CPNT-CRP-100331 JARDIANCE (v1.0)
Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-000964 | Match Text: In patients with CKD, JARDIANCE reduced the relative risk of first and recurrent all-cause hospitalisation by 14% | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Efficacy | Footnotes: In the EMPA-KIDNEY trial, a randomised,""" ;
    kg:token_count 300 .

