    kg:audience "HCP/Internal" ;
    kg:claim_status "candidate" ;
    kg:claim_text "The mechanism of action of JARDIANCE is dependent on blood glucose levels, meaning it only removes glucose when levels are elevated. The risk of hypoglycaemia only increases when it’s combined with other medications that can cause low blood sugar, such as insulin or sulphonylureas.2" ;
