<urn:kg:jardiance:section:0e91383f-891f-429a-ab40-686f5e3ffd27> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5d2dd211-4f5a-4030-bde4-1c43dd293e46> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 10 ;
    kg:section_id "0e91383f-891f-429a-ab40-686f5e3ffd27" ;
    kg:section_type "body" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """history of chronic or recurrent urinary tract infections were more likely to experience a urinary tract infection.  The rate of treatment discontinuation due to urinary tract infections was 0.1%, 0.2%, and 0.1% for placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg, respectively.

Urinary tract infections occurred more frequently in female patients.  The incidence of urinary tract infections in female patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg was 16.6%, 18.4%, and 17.0%, respectively.  The incidence of urinary tract infections in male patients randomized to placebo, JARDIANCE 10 mg, and JARDIANCE 25 mg was 3.2%, 3.6%, and 4.1%, respectively [see Use in Specific Populations (8.5)] .""" .

