    kg:section_title "16 HOW SUPPLIED/STORAGE AND HANDLING" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """JARDIANCE tablets are available as follows:

10 mg tablets: pale yellow, round, biconvex, and bevel-edged film-coated tablets debossed with 'S 10' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side.

Bottles of 30 (NDC 0597-0152-30)

Bottles of 90 (NDC 0597-0152-90)

Cartons containing 3 blister cards of 10 tablets each (3 x 10) (NDC 0597-0152-37), institutional pack.

25 mg tablets: pale yellow, oval, biconvex film-coated tablets, debossed with 'S 25' on one side and the Boehringer Ingelheim company symbol on the other side.

Bottles of 30 (NDC 0597-0153-30)

Bottles of 90 (NDC 0597-0153-90)

Cartons containing 3 blister cards of 10 tablets each (3 x 10) (NDC 0597-0153-37), institutional pack.

Dispense in a well-closed container as defined in the USP.

Storage

Store at 20°C to 25°C (68°F to 77°F); excursions permitted to 15°C to 30°C (59°F to 86°F) [see USP Controlled Room Temperature].""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:661eaa1b-0147-4b8d-9284-822350db014b> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c89ff6ba-39bc-440c-a80f-70a6656dc004> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 17 ;
    kg:section_id "661eaa1b-0147-4b8d-9284-822350db014b" ;
    kg:section_title "Pediatric Patients" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text "The pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of empagliflozin were investigated in pediatric patients aged 10 to 17 years with type 2 diabetes mellitus. Oral administration of empagliflozin at 10 mg and 25 mg resulted in exposure within the range observed in adult patients." .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ad8a6e97-fe65-4803-88da-8af832ce383d>,
        <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c4a9d2dc-34e9-431d-aa4d-cf3a1be2ad3b> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 67 ;
    kg:section_id "66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b" ;
    kg:section_title "Introduction to family branding" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:text """The global branding system applies to the 'JARDIANCE family' in a way that visually depicts the relationship between the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance and among its related product brands in the Diabetes Portfolio.

There are 3 products that comprise the JARDIANCE family, with JARDIANCE being the lead brand and SYNJARDY and GLYXAMBI as line extensions:

- JARDIANCE ®  (empagliflozin)
- SYNJARDY ®  (empagliflozin/metformin HCl)
- GLYXAMBI ®  (empagliflozin/linagliptin)

This section highlights the specific JARDIANCE family branding elements, explains the rationale behind them, and provides detailed instructions for approved use to ensure consistency throughout all communications.

<!-- image -->

Keep in mind that when any of the family brands are used in combination with JARDIANCE, the JARDIANCE branding elements (eg, colour, environment, page architecture) must be adhered to.

Important: please note that the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance is not currently pursuing future heart failure or chronic kidney disease indications for SYNJARDY or GLYXAMBI. There are no updates to design or branding on family brands.""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:678b0bd7-8669-4ae5-bf44-a37a85fedf3e> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
