    kg:section_title "p-value = 0.0040" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text "" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:a0d22c6f-3704-402a-8bef-b0039f4472c1> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:43d75440-26d7-48ab-a764-a63f48d7f763> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 1 ;
    kg:section_id "a0d22c6f-3704-402a-8bef-b0039f4472c1" ;
    kg:section_title "----------------------------INDICATIONS AND USAGE---------------------------" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0" ;
    kg:source_document_type "prescribing_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Jardiance_PI.pdf" ;
    kg:text """JARDIANCE is a sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor indicated:

- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure. (1)
- x To reduce the risk of sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression. (1)
- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease. (1)
- x As an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and pediatric patients aged 10 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus. (1)""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5323d531-2c7f-44f7-94de-ecd7a90ebbda>,
        <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:96c4477c-37cd-4e29-bc91-2381ebbf1a20> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 10 ;
    kg:section_id "a0ddb39b-c2b1-4561-99f1-7dc562743052" ;
    kg:section_title "Major hypoglycaemia (events requiring assistance)" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40" ;
    kg:source_document_type "product_information" ;
    kg:source_file_name "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:text """No increase in major hypoglycaemia was observed with empagliflozin compared to placebo as monotherapy, add-on to metformin, add-on to metformin and a sulphonylurea, add-on to pioglitazone with or without metformin, add-on to linagliptin and metformin, as adjunct to standard care therapy and for the combination of empagliflozin with metformin in drug-naïve patients compared to those treated with empagliflozin and metformin as individual components. An increased frequency was noted when given as add-on to basal insulin with or without metformin and with or without a sulphonylurea (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo: 0% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 0%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 1.3%, placebo 0% over the 78-week trial), and add-on to MDI insulin with or without metformin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 0.5%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 0.5% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 1.6%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 0.5%, placebo: 1.6% over the 52-week trial).

In the EMPEROR heart failure studies, major hypoglycaemia was observed at similar frequencies in patients with diabetes mellitus when treated with empagliflozin and placebo as add-on to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 2.2%, placebo: 1.9%).""" .

<urn:kg:jardiance:section:a13d3b4a-4fa5-486f-92ca-8e399085cf68> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:97cc29d2-be61-4d5d-b724-5f212f6b5af4> ;
