<urn:kg:jardiance:section:a3b8e037-fa73-4533-bfad-01239990e7ef> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:56a9dca4-628b-4cee-a0f3-f2ddd3a7910a> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 40 ;
    kg:section_id "a3b8e037-fa73-4533-bfad-01239990e7ef" ;
    kg:section_title "Page architecture" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b" ;
    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf" ;
    kg:text """Page architecture is an element of visual styling that allows the audience to readily identify a brand by sight.

Page architecture should draw on other branding elements, such as the symbol, to create a distinct look and feel that supports the intention of the communication.

It is important for the page architecture to demonstrate versatility and be flexible enough to work across a variety of media, including digital, print, and experiential. It should also allow for use in landscape and portrait formats for pieces as small as a postcard or as large as a billboard.""" .

