#: 104 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPEROR-Reduced trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 3730 patients with HFrEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=1863) were evaluated vs placebo (n=1867). Patients were adults with chronic HF (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR- Reduced trial was a composite of CV death or hospitalisation for HF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 25% RRR in this endpoint 
(HR=0.75; 95% CI: 0.65, 0.86; p<0.001). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29; 2026 PCP iVA p.111 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.21; 2026 Endo iVA p.24; 2026 PCP iVA p.29; 2026 PCP iVA p.111
#: 105 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPEROR-Preserved trial, a randomised, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled study of 5988 patients with HFpEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=2997) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2991). Patients were adults with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%). The primary endpoint in the EMPEROR-Preserved trial was a composite of CV death or HHF, analysed as time to the first event. Patients treated with JARDIANCE experienced a 21% RRR in this endpoint 
(HR=0.79; 95% CI: 0.69, 0.90; p<0.001). | Status: Corrected | Indication: Heart failure | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 40% | Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73; 2026 Card iVA p.104 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.25; 2026 Card iVA p.67; 2026 Card iVA p.70; 2026 Card iVA p.73; 2026 Card iVA p.104
