#: 173 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients of JARDIANCE. JARDIANCE should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes or for the treatment of DKA. JARDIANCE should be used with caution in patients who may be at a higher risk of ketoacidosis while taking JARDIANCE. In patients where DKA is suspected or diagnosed, treatment with JARDIANCE should be discontinued immediately. For use in patients with renal impairment, please refer to the dosing page of this document and the SmPC.1 | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardio-Renal, Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.54; 2026 Card iVA p.48; 2026 Card iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.120; 2026 PCP iVA p.51 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.54; 2026 Card iVA p.48; 2026 Card iVA p.91; 2026 Card iVA p.120; 2026 PCP iVA p.51
