Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001211 | Match Text: In adult patients with HF across the LVEF spectrum, JARDIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in hospital within 1-5 days after stabilization | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and reduced ejection fraction (LVEF ≤40%).  Adult patients with chronic heart failure (NYHA class II, III, or IV) and preserved ejection fraction (LVEF >40%).  In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054).   CI=confidence interval; KCCQ-TSS=Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Total Symptom Score; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; NYHA=New York Heart Association. | Reference: RD-157832 JARDIANCE M. Packer, S.D. Anker, J. Butler; Cardiovascular and Renal Outcomes with Empagli 

